    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a **400**.\n\nI routed the rule through the existing `OwnerFieldsValidator` \u2014 the Spring `Validator` already registered (via `@InitBinder`) for `OwnerFieldsDto` request bodies. Binding errors it raises flow through `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`, which already maps them to 400, so no new plumbing was needed.\n\nChange (single file, `OwnerFieldsValidator.java`):\n- Added a new cohesive private method `validateRegistrationDate(...)` mirroring the neighbouring `validatePostcode(...)` \u2014 it rejects `registrationDate` values `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`.\n- Added one call to it from `validate(...)` and one `import java.time.LocalDate`.\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: the only pre-existing method edited (`validate`) gained a single call line and no new branch (its cyclomatic complexity is unchanged), and the new logic lives in a small standalone unit rather than being grown inside the large `addOwner` controller method (whose class carries far higher surrounding complexity).\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` passes (payload `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` \u2192 400), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
